# Environment for `nx e2e server-e2e`.
#
# Nx loads `{projectRoot}/.env.<target>` for that target's task, so the command
# AGENTS.md documents — `npx nx e2e server-e2e` — carries this by itself. No
# wrapper script, nothing to remember, nothing to re-derive at minute 21.
#
# Committed on purpose, unlike `.env`: it holds a machine-shaped tuning number,
# not a secret and not a connection string. (`.gitignore` covers `.env`,
# `.env.local` and `.env.*.local` — not this.)

# Raise the old-space ceiling for the run.
#
# `jest.config.cts` pins `maxWorkers: 1`, and Jest reads that as "run in band":
# every spec executes in the task process itself rather than a worker, so there
# is one process for all ~94 files and nothing ever recycles it. Its heap climbs
# monotonically — each file boots its own Nest app in its own module registry —
# measured at 1.3 GB by 12 minutes and 2.0 GB by 25.
#
# Node sizes the default ceiling from total RAM: 2.2 GB on an 8 GB machine. A
# full run reaches that around minute 20 and dies with "Ineffective mark-compacts
# near heap limit", attributed to whichever suite happened to be running — a
# crash that looks like a spec and is not one.
#
# This is a ceiling, not a reservation. Node commits only what it touches, so
# the number costs a short run nothing; it only decides how far a long one gets.
NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=4096
